9	//     addresses immediately before and after the range are not.
10	//   - 192.0.129.7/17 admits exactly 192.0.128.0 - 192.0.255.255 (the boundary
11	//     sits inside the third octet), with the same edge behavior.
12	//   - 192.0.2.3/31 is the two-address network 192.0.2.2 - 192.0.2.3: both
13	//     addresses take part in filtering — neither is set aside as a network or
14	//     broadcast address — while 192.0.2.1 and 192.0.2.4 stay out.
15	//
